    spacex_q3_2026_guide_q4_capex_vs_q3: {"v": null, "lo": 1.79, "hi": 2.04, "unit": "multiple", "display": "1.8× to 2.0×", "label": "Q4 capex guidance against Q3 capex", "tier": "C", "src": "bw", "asOf": "2026-12-31", "on": "2026-10-25", "hatched": true, "basis": "times Q3 capex", "note": "'Roughly double its capital spending this quarter' (facts review WARN 15).", "url": "https://ir.spacex.com/"},
    spacex_q3_2026_guide_q1_2027_revenue_vs_q3: {"v": null, "lo": 2.26, "hi": 2.54, "unit": "multiple", "display": "2.3× to 2.5×", "label": "Q1 2027 revenue guidance against Q3 revenue", "tier": "C", "src": "bw", "asOf": "2027-03-31", "on": "2026-10-25", "hatched": true, "basis": "times Q3 revenue", "note": "'More than double'. A guide over an actual.", "url": "https://ir.spacex.com/"},
    spacex_q3_2026_cfo_payback_and_pricing: {"v": null, "unit": "text", "display": "At current pricing, new compute deployments are generating a payback of less than a year. Pricing is currently tracking slightly above the high end of the $30 to $50 per watt range we were discussing just last quarter", "label": "the CFO on payback and pricing", "tier": "P", "src": "spacex_q3_webcast", "asOf": "2026-10-20", "on": "2026-10-20", "note": "Bret Johnsen, CFO (clip 6). His claim. The unit behind 'per watt' (a year, or the contract) is not stated. Transcript at ir.spacex.com (no direct file URL resolved 25 Oct); local copy read 25 Oct. Quote cards follow this… (ledger)", "url": "https://ir.spacex.com/"},
    spacex_q3_2026_musk_yankees: {"v": null, "unit": "text", "display": "This is a bit like the New York Yankees playing in Little League. It's not fair.", "label": "Musk on the competition", "tier": "P", "src": "spacex_q3_webcast", "asOf": "2026-10-20", "on": "2026-10-20", "note": "Elon Musk (clip 1). Said of 'a team' applied 'to the deployment of terrestrial compute'; the sentence before starts 'A team'. Transcript at ir.spacex.com (no direct file URL resolved 25 Oct); local copy read 25 Oct. Quot… (ledger)", "url": "https://ir.spacex.com/"},
    spacex_q3_2026_musk_arr_forecast_2027: {"v": null, "lo": 500000, "hi": 1000000, "unit": "USD millions", "display": "$500B to $1T", "label": "Musk's forecast: annual recurring revenue, end 2027", "tier": "P", "src": "spacex_q3_webcast", "asOf": "2027-12-31", "on": "2026-10-20", "hatched": true, "basis": "USD millions (ARR, end-2027)", "note": "Elon Musk (clip 2). P as a statement; a FORECAST, his own, not company guidance (the CFO's goal is $100B by Dec 2026). The audio says 'a trillion'. Transcript at ir.spacex.com (no direct file URL resolved 25 Oct); local … (ledger)", "url": "https://ir.spacex.com/"},
    spacex_q3_2026_musk_compute_targets: {"v": 13, "unit": "GW", "display": "13 GW+", "label": "Musk's forecast: compute online, end 2027", "tier": "P", "src": "spacex_q3_webcast", "asOf": "2027-12-31", "on": "2026-10-20", "hatched": true, "basis": "GW (compute online, end-2027; his floor)", "note": "Elon Musk (clip 4). A forecast. Also: 'a small possibility at this point, but it's not zero -- of SpaceX having over 20 gigawatts' online next year. CFO: 'nearly 2 GW' at end-October, 2.5-3 GW by end-2026. Transcript at … (ledger)", "url": "https://ir.spacex.com/"},
    spacex_q3_2026_musk_spot_market_rent: {"v": null, "unit": "text", "display": "as a rough approximation, our goal is to kind of split it 50-50, more or less, where half of the compute is used internally and half of it is rented to others. ... rent at effectively the spot-market rate, as opposed to signing these long-term deals.", "label": "Musk on what SpaceX rents out", "tier": "P", "src": "spacex_q3_webcast", "asOf": "2026-10-20", "on": "2026-10-20", "note": "Elon Musk (clip 9). The 50-50 split is the scenarios' 'share rented' driver. Transcript at ir.spacex.com (no direct file URL resolved 25 Oct); local copy read 25 Oct. Quote cards follow this text, captions the audio.", "url": "https://ir.spacex.com/"},
    spacex_q3_2026_musk_renewals_higher: {"v": null, "unit": "text", "display": "And we see them renewing at higher dollars per watt, not lower dollars per watt.", "label": "Musk on renewals", "tier": "P", "src": "spacex_q3_webcast", "asOf": "2026-10-20", "on": "2026-10-20", "note": "Elon Musk. His claim; no figure given. Transcript at ir.spacex.com (no direct file URL resolved 25 Oct); local copy read 25 Oct. Quote cards follow this text, captions the audio.", "url": "https://ir.spacex.com/"},
    spacex_q3_2026_musk_demand_claims: {"v": null, "unit": "text", "display": "We are also, frankly, hounded relentlessly by every hyperscaler and by dozens of smaller companies to rent more of our compute. We could rent out our compute several times over if we said yes to everyone.", "label": "Musk on demand", "tier": "P", "src": "spacex_q3_webcast", "asOf": "2026-10-20", "on": "2026-10-20", "note": "Elon Musk (clip 10). His claims. The tag: 'I'm not saying this will happen. It's not impossible that we will have a six-month payback period for compute next year.' Keep 'I'm not saying this will happen' if it is in the … (ledger)", "url": "https://ir.spacex.com/"},
    spacex_q3_2026_musk_merger_remark: {"v": null, "unit": "text", "display": "I think some people out there assume that a SpaceX and Tesla merger is a certainty, and I think that would be overstating it.", "label": "Musk on a Tesla merger", "tier": "P", "src": "spacex_q3_webcast", "asOf": "2026-10-20", "on": "2026-10-20", "note": "Elon Musk (optional clip 11). He goes on: 'Do I think it would be a good idea? Yes.' Transcript at ir.spacex.com (no direct file URL resolved 25 Oct); local copy read 25 Oct. Quote cards follow this text, captions the au… (ledger)", "url": "https://ir.spacex.com/"},
